<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
<title>News ideas</title>
<meta name="robots" content="noindex">
<link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/style.css">
<style>
  body { padding: 2.5rem var(--gutter) 4rem; }
  h1 { font-size: var(--fs-heading); font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: -.03em; margin-bottom: .4rem; }
  .lede { color: var(--muted); margin-bottom: 2rem; max-width: 46rem; }
  .grid4 { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: 2.5rem 2rem; }
  .frame { position: relative; height: 540px; overflow: hidden; border: var(--border); background: var(--bg);
    background-image: radial-gradient(var(--dots) 1px, transparent 1.2px); background-size: 16px 16px; }
  .label { position: absolute; left: 14px; top: 12px; z-index: 5; font-family: var(--mono); font-size: var(--fs-mono); color: var(--quiet); }
  .label b { color: var(--ink); font-weight: 500; }
  .about { margin-top: .7rem; font-size: var(--fs-small); color: var(--muted); max-width: 40rem; }

  /* shared: readable news text, never moving */
  .item { font-size: var(--fs-small); line-height: 1.55; color: var(--ink); }
  .item strong { color: var(--strong); }
  .when { font-family: var(--mono); font-size: var(--fs-mono); color: var(--quiet); display: block; margin-bottom: .15rem; }

  /* objects (sketched with CSS here; 3D objects on the real page) */
  .o { position: absolute; border-radius: 50%; animation: bob 4.8s ease-in-out infinite; }
  .o.clay { background: radial-gradient(circle at 35% 30%, #fff, #ecebe7 45%, #c6c5c1 100%); }
  .o.steel { background: radial-gradient(circle at 35% 30%, #e8eef9, #b2c1d9 50%, #8495b2 100%); }
  .o.ink { background: radial-gradient(circle at 35% 30%, #6b6b73, #2a2a2e 50%, #0e0e10 100%); }
  .o.cube { border-radius: 22%; animation: bob 4.8s ease-in-out infinite, turn 9s linear infinite; }
  .o.ring { background: none; border: 7px solid #e7e6e2; box-shadow: inset 2px 2px 3px rgba(0,0,0,.12), 2px 2px 4px rgba(0,0,0,.1); }
  @keyframes bob { 50% { transform: translateY(-7px); } }
  @keyframes turn { to { rotate: 360deg; } }

  /* A — objects as markers */
  .A { position: absolute; left: 70px; right: 40px; top: 70px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 1.35rem; }
  .A .row { position: relative; padding-left: 64px; min-height: 40px; }
  .A .row .o { left: 0; top: 2px; width: 40px; height: 40px; }

  /* B — one object visits the item you are reading */
  .B { position: absolute; left: 110px; right: 40px; top: 70px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 1.35rem; }
  .B .row { opacity: .38; transition: opacity .45s ease; }
  .B .row.on { opacity: 1; }
  .visitor { position: absolute; left: 44px; width: 44px; height: 44px; transition: top .9s cubic-bezier(.3, .9, .2, 1); }

  /* C — one at a time */
  .C .big { position: absolute; left: 70px; top: 150px; width: 150px; height: 150px; }
  .C .queue .o { width: 34px; height: 34px; opacity: .6; filter: blur(.6px); }
  .C .note { position: absolute; left: 260px; right: 50px; top: 160px; }
  .C .note .item { font-size: var(--fs-lead); line-height: 1.4; transition: opacity .35s ease, transform .5s cubic-bezier(.2, .8, .1, 1); }
  .C .note .item.out { opacity: 0; transform: translateY(14px); }
  .C .dots { position: absolute; left: 260px; top: 400px; display: flex; gap: 8px; }
  .C .dots i { width: 7px; height: 7px; border-radius: 50%; background: var(--line); opacity: .25; }
  .C .dots i.on { opacity: 1; }

  /* D — notes tied to objects, in a tidy column */
  .D .o { position: absolute; }
  .D .tie { position: absolute; height: 1.5px; background: var(--ink); transform-origin: 0 50%; }
  .D .tie::before { content: ''; position: absolute; left: -4px; top: -3.25px; width: 8px; height: 8px; border-radius: 50%; background: var(--accent); }
  .D .col { position: absolute; left: 280px; right: 36px; top: 70px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 1.3rem; }
  .D .col { gap: 0; } .D .col .item { min-height: 112px; }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<h1>News, readable first</h1>
<p class="lede">Second round. In every version the text sits still, upright and in normal sentences; only the objects move. The objects are sketched flat here; on the page they are the real 3D ones.</p>

{% set items = news.slice(0, 4) %}
<div class="grid4">

  <div>
    <div class="frame"><p class="label"><b>A</b> · objects as markers</p>
      <div class="A">
        {% set tones = ['clay', 'steel', 'ink', 'clay'] %}
        {% for item in items %}
        <div class="row">
          <span class="o {{ tones[loop.index0] }}{% if loop.index0 == 1 %} cube{% endif %}{% if loop.index0 == 3 %} ring{% endif %}" style="animation-delay: -{{ loop.index0 * 1.2 }}s"></span>
          <p class="item"><span class="when">{{ item.date | monthName }} {{ item.date | yearOf }}</span>{{ item.text | newsText | safe }}</p>
        </div>
        {% endfor %}
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="about">A calm list; each news item has its own small 3D object beside it that bobs and turns. The quietest option, and fully readable.</p>
  </div>

  <div>
    <div class="frame" id="fb"><p class="label"><b>B</b> · one object visits what you read</p>
      <div class="B">
        {% for item in items %}
        <div class="row{% if loop.first %} on{% endif %}"><p class="item"><span class="when">{{ item.date | monthName }} {{ item.date | yearOf }}</span>{{ item.text | newsText | safe }}</p></div>
        {% endfor %}
      </div>
      <span class="o steel visitor" id="visitor" style="top: 72px"></span>
    </div>
    <p class="about">The same list; one object travels down beside it as you scroll, stops at the item you are reading and lights it up. (Here it steps on its own.)</p>
  </div>

  <div>
    <div class="frame C" id="fc"><p class="label"><b>C</b> · one at a time</p>
      <span class="o clay big"></span>
      <div class="queue">
        <span class="o steel" style="left: 245px; top: 90px"></span>
        <span class="o ink" style="left: 300px; top: 70px; animation-delay: -1s"></span>
        <span class="o clay" style="left: 355px; top: 92px; animation-delay: -2s"></span>
      </div>
      <div class="note">
        {% for item in items %}<p class="item" data-c="{{ loop.index0 }}" {% if not loop.first %}hidden{% endif %}><span class="when">{{ item.date | monthName }} {{ item.date | yearOf }}</span>{{ item.text | newsText | safe }}</p>{% endfor %}
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="about">The newest note large next to a big object; the rest wait as small objects behind it. Scrolling brings the next one forward. (Here it advances on its own.)</p>
  </div>

  <div>
    <div class="frame D"><p class="label"><b>D</b> · notes beside their objects</p>
      <span class="o clay" style="left: 150px; top: 64px; width: 84px; height: 84px"></span>
      <span class="o steel cube" style="left: 175px; top: 190px; width: 58px; height: 58px; animation-delay: -1.3s"></span>
      <span class="o ink" style="left: 168px; top: 300px; width: 66px; height: 66px; animation-delay: -2.4s"></span>
      <span class="o clay ring" style="left: 185px; top: 420px; width: 46px; height: 46px; animation-delay: -3.1s"></span>
      <div class="col" id="dcol">
        {% for item in items %}<p class="item"><span class="when">{{ item.date | monthName }} {{ item.date | yearOf }}</span>{{ item.text | newsText | safe }}</p>{% endfor %}
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="about">Closest to your favourite: each note sits right beside its own object, the objects at different sizes and depths, the notes lined up in one clean column. No lines connecting them.</p>
  </div>
</div>

<script>
// B: the visitor steps through the list
(() => {
  const f = document.getElementById('fb'), rows = [...f.querySelectorAll('.B .row')], v = document.getElementById('visitor');
  let k = 0;
  setInterval(() => {
    k = (k + 1) % rows.length;
    rows.forEach((r, i) => r.classList.toggle('on', i === k));
    v.style.top = (rows[k].offsetTop + 70 + 2) + 'px';
  }, 2600);
})();
// C: one note at a time
(() => {
  const f = document.getElementById('fc'), items = [...f.querySelectorAll('.note .item')];
  let k = 0;
  setInterval(() => {
    items[k].classList.add('out');
    setTimeout(() => {
      items[k].hidden = true; items[k].classList.remove('out');
      k = (k + 1) % items.length;
      items[k].classList.add('out'); items[k].hidden = false;
      requestAnimationFrame(() => requestAnimationFrame(() => items[k].classList.remove('out')));
    }, 350);
  }, 3600);
})();
</script>
</body>
</html>
